Aus raider #119. Net::Async::HTTP folgt GET-Redirects mit allen Headern; LWP entfernt nur Authorization, x-api-key bleibt. Dadurch kann der API-Key einer Engine über list_models an einen fremden Origin gehen. Repro: Langertha::Engine::Anthropic->new(url=>'https://a.example', api_key=>'k')->list_models gegen einen Server, der mit 307 auf https://b.example antwortet; b.example bekommt 'x-api-key: k'. Kontrollfall in langertha-raider t/70_cli_provider_run.t. Gewünscht: Bei einem Cross-Origin-Redirect alle Credential-Header entfernen (Authorization, x-api-key, x-goog-api-key, Key-Query-Parameter) oder Requests mit Credentials nicht redirecten. Beide HTTP-Pfade (LWP sync, Net::Async::HTTP async) abdecken, mit Test über einen lokalen HTTP-Fixture-Server.

2026-09-30 07:30 Findings: LWP 6.83 strips only Authorization on cross-origin redirect (older LWP nothing) -> x-api-key and any other header leak on sync. Net::Async::HTTP 0.50 does NOT carry request headers (builds a fresh GET from Location), so the header leak claim was sync-only; but on both transports an echoed Location query (?key=) leaks Gemini/AKI keys, and on NaHTTP a same-origin redirect LOSES the credential (parity gap), and a relative Location from https resolves to http://. POST redirects are followed by neither client (GET/HEAD only) -> AKI key-in-body is not re-sent. Mechanism: one policy module Langertha::HTTP::Redirect (same origin: unchanged; other origin: allowlist of representation headers only, userinfo dropped, query values equal to credentials the chain carried dropped, refuse if a credential would still be in the URL; GET/HEAD only; no https->http). Sync: default user_agent is Langertha::HTTP::UserAgent (MooseX::NonMoose extends LWP::UserAgent, redirect_ok hook). Async NaHTTP: max_redirects=>0 + hop-by-hop in _async_do_request_f. Test t/45_redirect_credentials.t red before (sync x-api-key, Gemini key all backends, async same-origin), green after; 10 mutants killed.

